-- title:
--   Toric dichotomy for J₀(Nq) at the monodromy toric part
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ and $q$ be nonzero natural numbers with $q$ prime and $q \nmid N$. Assume the Hecke inputs hold at every prime level for $Nq$ and for $N$ (`HeckeInputsAll`, i.e. for each prime $\ell$ the integrality, finiteness, fundamental-identity and norm-formula data of the $\ell$-th Hecke correspondence) and that the operators `heckeOperatorBar` commute pairwise in both levels; let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$, and let $S$ be a finite set of primes containing every prime divisor of $Nq$. Write $J = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the base-changed modular function field of level $Nq$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, with its Hecke module structure over $\mathbb T = \mathbb Z[T_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$, and let $I$ be the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$. The conclusion is the guarded dichotomy: for every maximal ideal $\mathfrak m \subset \mathbb T$ that is not eventually Eisenstein (there is no finite set of primes outside which $T_\ell - (\ell+1) \in \mathfrak m$) and for which $q$ is a unit in $\mathbb T/\mathfrak m$, every $x \in J$ annihilated by $\mathfrak m$ and fixed by all $\sigma \in I$ either lies in the $\mathbb T$-span of the elements $\sigma \cdot y - y$ with $\sigma \in I$ and $y \in J$ killed by some positive integer coprime to $q$, or else the predicate `HasLowerLevelTorsion S 𝔪 (ModularCurve.JZero N)` holds.
--
--   This is Ribet's geometric dichotomy at the prime $q$ for $J_0(Nq)$, with the toric part replaced by the explicit monodromy submodule generated by differences $\sigma y - y$ on torsion prime to $q$. It is the input to the comparison of ranks of the monodromy span and, through that, to the level-lowering step that produces lower-level torsion in $J_0(N)$ from a congruence of newforms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_toricDichotomy_toricMonodromyPart_jZero.lean

